---
import { customers, classes, reservations, instructors } from './model.mjs';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="a03-classes" aria-labelledby="a03-tables-title">
  <figcaption><span class="eyebrow">Figure {number} · the starting rows, as loaded into PostgreSQL 18.6</span><strong id="a03-tables-title">Classes, bookings and instructors</strong><span>The starting rows for every example: two classes, one existing booking and two instructors for class 21. <span class="tag key">PK</span> marks primary-key columns and <span class="tag ref">FK</span> a column that must match another table’s key.</span></figcaption>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="box wide">
      <table>
        <caption><code>classes</code> · one row per class</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">class_id <span class="tag key">PK</span></th><th scope="col">title</th><th scope="col">capacity</th><th scope="col">remaining</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{classes.map(r => <tr><td class="key">{r.class_id}</td><td>{r.title}</td><td>{r.capacity}</td><td class="mark">{r.remaining}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="box">
      <table>
        <caption><code>customers</code></caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">customer_id <span class="tag key">PK</span></th><th scope="col">name</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{customers.map(r => <tr><td class="key">{r.customer_id}</td><td>{r.name}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="box">
      <table>
        <caption><code>reservations</code> · one row per booked place</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">request_id <span class="tag key">PK</span></th><th scope="col">class_id <span class="tag ref">FK</span></th><th scope="col">owner_id <span class="tag ref">FK</span></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{reservations.map(r => <tr><td class="key">{r.request_id}</td><td class="ref">{r.class_id}</td><td class="ref">{r.owner_id}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note"><code>UNIQUE (class_id, owner_id)</code>: one booking per customer per class. Tariq (customer 2) holds R7 in class 22.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="box">
      <table>
        <caption><code>instructors</code> · who can teach a class</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">class_id <span class="tag key">PK</span> <span class="tag ref">FK</span></th><th scope="col">person <span class="tag key">PK</span></th><th scope="col">available</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{instructors.map(r => <tr><td class="key ref">{r.class_id}</td><td class="key">{r.person}</td><td>{String(r.available)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="rules"><strong>Rules the examples protect.</strong> For each class, <code>remaining</code> plus its bookings equals <code>capacity</code>. A customer books a class at most once. Class 21 keeps at least one available instructor.</p>
</figure>
<style is:global>
  figure.a03-classes { margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1.2rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); background: var(--color-surface-alt); }
  figure.a03-classes figcaption { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  figure.a03-classes figcaption span, figure.a03-classes figcaption strong { display: block; } figure.a03-classes figcaption .tag { display: inline-block; }
  figure.a03-classes figcaption strong { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: .3rem; }
  figure.a03-classes .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(17rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: .8rem; }
  figure.a03-classes .box.wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  figure.a03-classes .box { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background: var(--color-surface); padding: .6rem; }
  figure.a03-classes table { display: table; width: 100%; margin: 0; border-collapse: collapse; font: .78rem/1.45 var(--font-mono); }
  figure.a03-classes caption { text-align: left; font: 600 .82rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); padding-bottom: .45rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  figure.a03-classes th, figure.a03-classes td { border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: .35rem .45rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: bottom; }
  figure.a03-classes th { background: none; font-weight: 600; }
  figure.a03-classes .tag { display: inline-block; font: 600 .62rem/1.3 var(--font-sans); padding: .05rem .3rem; border-radius: .2rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  figure.a03-classes .tag.key { background: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-surface); }
  figure.a03-classes .tag.ref { border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-accent-strong); }
  figure.a03-classes td.key { font-weight: 700; }
  figure.a03-classes td.ref { text-decoration: underline dashed var(--color-accent); text-underline-offset: .25em; }
  figure.a03-classes td.mark { font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-accent-strong); }
  figure.a03-classes .note, figure.a03-classes .rules { font-size: .8rem; margin: .6rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  figure.a03-classes .rules { margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--color-text); font-size: .85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { figure.a03-classes { padding: .6rem; } figure.a03-classes .box { padding: .35rem; } figure.a03-classes table { font-size: .7rem; } figure.a03-classes th, figure.a03-classes td { padding: .3rem .25rem; } }
</style>
